    "faq_zG3iEx": {
      "type": "faq",
      "blocks": {
        "question_eqPWnn": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Who is the A1 designed for?",
            "text": "<p>A1 is designed for professionals who carry more than just a laptop. Its 26L layout is built around multiple devices, work documents, chargers, personal essentials and light 1–2 night travel—making it especially suited to business commuters, consultants, managers, sales professionals and frequent business travelers.</p>",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "question_VzHDrA": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "What makes A1 different from a regular business backpack?",
            "text": "<p>A1 is built as a complete business carry system rather than a single-compartment laptop backpack. Dedicated zones separate your devices, work materials, quick-access essentials and personal items, so you can move between the office, client meetings, airports and short trips without constantly reorganizing your bag.</p>",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "question_faQPjM": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Is 26L too large for everyday work?",
            "text": "<p>Not necessarily. A1 uses its 26L capacity across dedicated compartments rather than one oversized main cavity, helping it stay organized for everyday work while leaving room for days when you carry more. You can use it for your regular laptop-and-office setup without needing to fill the entire bag.</p>",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "question_XgrxRi": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "What can I carry in the A1 for a typical workday?",
            "text": "<p>A1 is designed to carry a laptop, tablet, chargers, cables, documents, notebooks, headphones and everyday personal items in separate, organized zones. The layout helps keep work equipment easy to find instead of stacking everything together in one compartment.</p>",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "question_CUVMab": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Can the A1 handle a 1–2 night business trip?",
            "text": "<p>Yes. The 26L capacity is designed to bridge everyday work and light business travel. Alongside your work setup, there is room for compact clothing and personal essentials for a short 1–2 night trip, helping you avoid carrying a separate work bag and travel bag for lighter trips.</p>",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "question_ymcQ63": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "What size laptop fits in the A1?",
            "text": "<p>A1 is designed for most 14–16\" laptops, depending on the device’s exact dimensions and protective case. Its dedicated rear device compartment separates your laptop and other tech from the main packing area while adding structured impact protection.</p>",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "question_EGAYmQ": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "How does A1 protect multiple devices?",
            "text": "<p>The rear device compartment keeps your laptop, tablet and work tech separate from clothing and everyday items. Structured padding, including EVA protection and a supportive back panel, helps reduce everyday bumps while keeping high-value devices securely organized during commutes and travel.</p>",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "question_Hg84Xe": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Is the A1 comfortable when fully loaded?",
            "text": "<p>Yes. Despite its structured 1.7 kg build, A1 carries comfortably thanks to adjustable padded shoulder straps, a stabilizing chest strap and a breathable, cushioned back panel that help distribute weight and keep the bag close to your body. The result is a more balanced, supported feel even when carrying multiple devices and a full work setup.</p>",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "question_BN6grY": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Can I use the A1 as a carry-on?",
            "text": "<p>A1 measures approximately 29 × 49 × 18 cm and is designed with business travel in mind. It can work well as a compact carry-on for many trips, but airline size requirements vary, so we recommend checking your airline’s current cabin baggage limits before departure.</p>",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "question_LqC4FC": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Should I choose A1 if I only carry a laptop and a few small items?",
            "text": "<p>If your daily carry is very minimal, A1 may offer more organization and capacity than you need. A1 makes the most sense for people who regularly carry multiple devices, documents, chargers and personal items—or want one bag that can move from daily business use into short work trips.</p>",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        }
      },
